class:: AVbind
summary:: Pbind that plays an audio note AND a synchronised visual
categories:: Libraries>VisualServer
related:: Classes/Vbind, Classes/Pbind, Guides/VisualServer, Reference/VisualParameters

description::

Factory returning a link::Classes/Pbind:: pre-seeded with code::(type: \audioVisual, dur: 1, instrument: \default, view: \default)::. Each event first plays the audio note (using code::\instrument::, code::\freq::, code::\amp::, code::\dur:: ... as a normal code::\note::), then builds and plays a separate visual event routed to the correct visual sub-type by code::\vinstrument::.

Visual parameters are prefixed with strong::v:: so they do not collide with audio keys:

table::
## strong::audio-visual key:: || strong::maps to visual:: || strong::default
## code::\vinstrument:: || the visual def || code::\circle::
## code::\vview:: || code::\view:: || code::\default::
## code::\vdur:: || visual code::\dur:: || code::~dur::
## code::\vx \vy:: || code::\x \y:: || code::~x ? 0::
## code::\vsize:: || code::\size:: || code::(~amp ? 0.5) * 100::
## code::\vcolor:: || code::\color:: || from code::~freq:: hue
## code::\vx1 \vy1 \vx2 \vy2:: || line endpoints || -0.5/0/0.5/0
::
Pulse keys (code::\startSize \endSize \curve::) and code::\width:: pass through directly.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: new
argument:: ... pairs
Audio + code::v::-prefixed visual pairs.
returns:: a link::Classes/Pbind::.

EXAMPLES::

code::
s.boot;
AVbind(
    \instrument, \default,
    \freq, Pseq([440,550,660,880], inf),
    \amp, 0.2, \dur, 0.5,
    \vinstrument, \pulse,
    \vx, Pkey(\freq).linlin(440, 880, -0.7, 0.7),
    \endSize, Pkey(\amp) * 600,
    \vdur, 1.2,
    \vview, \demo
).play;
::

note:: code::AVbind:: is played with code::.play:: (it drives audio + visual via the event system), not code::.vplay::. ::
